      ],
      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "buildJavaScript": "Follow these strict rules when generating code: do not use loops or arrays, do not use function parameters, and absolutely avoid all logical operators including NOT (!), AND (&&), and OR (||). All conditional logic must be written using strictly nested if/else statements; do not use else if chains. Use explicit boolean comparisons (e.g., if (conditionA === true)). Place all logic exclusively inside the existing updateAppUI arrow function, evaluating only the provided global variables conditionA and conditionB. The logic paths, text messages, and image URLs must be based entirely and exactly on the flowchart or prompt provided by the student. Update the UI directly inside the nested blocks by assigning values to adMessage.innerText and adBackground.src. Completely ignore lab-overlay.js and any HTML/CSS associated with the testing lab overlay; do not generate or modify any code related to it. You must write the complete updateAppUI function covering all four possible outcomes explicitly; do not provide a partial implementation or leave placeholders."
      }
    },
    "bubble_choice_description": "Use your plan to build a function that updates what is featured based on the inputs you designed.",
    "long_instructions": "## Build Your Function with AI\r\nBuild a function that updates what is featured based on the inputs you planned.\r\n\r\n1. **Build**\r\n   - Import your Sketch from your Backpack and give it to AI Tutor as context.\r\n   - Use your plan to write a prompt for AI Tutor to generate your function.\r\n\r\n2. **Test**\r\n   - Click different title buttons.\r\n   - Does the featured display update based on what you clicked?\r\n\r\n3. **Check Code**\r\n   - Where are the inputs (parameters) defined?\r\n   - Where are they used in the function?\r\n   - Where is the function called?",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/87734f71086b60ecb27a6c1fbe52e06e-hero-default.jpg"
  },
